# No Git LFS in this repository, deliberately.
#
# The model was previously tracked with LFS, which broke deployment: Streamlit
# Community Cloud clones without resolving LFS objects, so the app received a
# 134-byte pointer file where it expected a 147 MiB model. slim_model.py strips
# the unused Adam optimiser state from the .keras archive (147 -> 68 MiB), which
# brings it under GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit and lets it be committed as an
# ordinary binary. Do not re-add an LFS filter for *.keras.

# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF, while still checking out
# native endings on Windows. Without this, files committed from Windows differ
# from the same files committed from Linux and show up as spuriously modified.
* text=auto

# Binary: never translate line endings, never attempt a textual diff.
*.keras binary
*.h5    binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary

# Notebooks are JSON with embedded output cells. Textual diffs of them are
# unreadable and enormous, so suppress them; the file is still versioned.
*.ipynb -diff

# Keep GitHub's language statistics meaningful — without this the repo is
# reported as mostly Jupyter Notebook rather than Python.
*.ipynb linguist-documentation
